Name: maxheaderlines
Type: INT
Default-Value: 1000
Last-Modified: UNRELEASED

Maximum number of headers that will be processed into cache records.
Default 1000.  If set to zero, it is unlimited.  A header counts once,
however many lines it is folded over.  If a message hits the limit, an
error will be logged and the rest of the headers will be skipped.  This is
to avoid malformed messages causing giant cache records.
